nal Symposium on Antarctic Earth Sciences, New Zealand J. Geol. Geophys., Royal Society of New Zealand, in press.</li><li class="ordered-list--item ds2-5-body-md">C.J. Pudsey, Sedimentation on the continental rise west of the Antarctic Peninsula over the last three glacial cycles, Mar. Geol. 167 (2000) 313^338.</li><li class="ordered-list--item ds2-5-body-md">A. Camerlenghi, A. Crise, C.J. Pudsey, E. Accerboni, R. Laterza, M. Rebesco, Ten-month observation of the bot- tom current regime across a sediment drift of the Paci¢c margin of the Antarctic Peninsula, Antarct. Sci. 9 (4) (1997) 424^431.</li><li class="ordered-list--item ds2-5-body-md">M.J. Dekkers, Magnetic properties of natural pyrrhotite Part I: Behaviour of initial susceptibility and saturationm agnetization-related rock-magnetic parameters in a grain-size dependent framework, Phys. Earth Planet. In- ter. 52 (1988) 376^393.</li><li class="ordered-list--item ds2-5-body-md">M.J. Dekkers, Magnetic properties of natural pyrrhotite II: High-and low-temperature behavior of J rs and TRM as a function of grain size, Phys. Earth Planet. Inter. 57 (1989) 266^283.</li><li class="ordered-list--item ds2-5-body-md">D. Paillard, L. Labeyrie, P. Yiou, Macintosh program performing time-series analysis, EOS Trans. AGU 77 (1996) 379.</li><li class="ordered-list--item ds2-5-body-md">C. Laj, C. Kissel, A. Mazaud, J.E.T. Channel, J. Beer, North Atlantic paleointensity stack since 75 ka (NAPIS- 75) and the duration of the Laschamp event, Phil. Trans. R. Soc. Lond. A 358 (2000) 1009^1025.</li><li class="ordered-list--item ds2-5-body-md">E. Tric et al., Paleointensity of the geomagnetic ¢eld dur- ing the last eighty thousand years, J. Geophys. Res. 97 (1992) 9337^9351.</li><li class="ordered-list--item ds2-5-body-md">L. Meynadier, J.-P. Valet, R. Weeks, N.J. Shackleton, V.L. Hagee, Relative geomagnetic intensity of the ¢eld during the last 140 ka, Earth Planet. Sci. Lett. 114 (1992) 39^57.</li><li class="ordered-list--item ds2-5-b